1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,700
I'm Pluto;

2
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:02,200
I built ExitPlan alone.

3
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:09,700
This is my own hedge: two SOL in my wallet, two SOL short on Hyperliquid, a hundred dollars in Kamino.

4
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:13,075
I need three hundred dollars out without breaking it.

5
00:00:13,125 --> 00:00:14,575
Here's what ExitPlan checks.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,394
Net exposure: zero SOL.

7
00:00:16,444 --> 00:00:18,561
Two SOL spot, two SOL short.

8
00:00:18,611 --> 00:00:22,894
Hyperliquid's withdrawable, next to my model's buffer: same figure, to the cent.

9
00:00:22,944 --> 00:00:25,061
Account mode: standard, verified on HyperCore.

10
00:00:25,111 --> 00:00:27,228
Public APIs, no keys, no custody.

11
00:00:27,278 --> 00:00:31,561
Keep my SOL is on, and I ask for three hundred dollars.

12
00:00:31,611 --> 00:00:32,283
No route.

13
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:36,978
Every route that sells SOL is rejected: it breaks the rule I set.

14
00:00:37,028 --> 00:00:39,867
I allow selling SOL but keep net exposure.

15
00:00:39,917 --> 00:00:45,283
A paired trim appears: sell about one point four SOL, buy back the same short.

16
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:51,783
Net exposure stays zero, liquidation moves from here to here, and this is the carry I give up.

17
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:52,433
Rehearsal.

18
00:00:52,194 --> 00:00:52,867
Hyperliquid first:

19
00:00:52,917 --> 00:01:00,089
I preview the fill on the live book: average price, my own taker fee, cost against the plan, book age.

20
00:01:00,139 --> 00:01:04,061
And this is the inner reduce-only IOC order I would sign.

21
00:01:04,111 --> 00:01:05,144
Built, never sent.

22
00:01:05,194 --> 00:01:08,756
Kamino: the real withdrawal, built with Kamino's SDK and simulated.

23
00:01:08,806 --> 00:01:11,644
It would deliver exactly what the plan says.

24
00:01:11,694 --> 00:01:15,256
Jupiter: the real swap for my wallet, run through simulateTransaction.

25
00:01:15,306 --> 00:01:19,950
It passes, and here is the unsigned transaction, decoded in Solana Explorer's inspector.

26
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,950
Everything runs in the browser against public endpoints:

27
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,075
Solana RPC, the Kamino API, Jupiter, and the Hyperliquid info API.

28
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:28,575
No keys, no custody.

29
00:01:28,625 --> 00:01:36,075
Two small Vercel functions: one builds and simulates the real Kamino withdrawal; one turns plain English into a constraint proposal.

30
00:01:36,125 --> 00:01:37,200
Challenge one, margin.

31
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:39,825
Hyperliquid's withdrawable is not equity minus maintenance.

32
00:01:39,875 --> 00:01:49,575
I reserve margin with the exchange's transfer rule, the larger of initial margin and ten percent of notional, and check it against the exchange's own withdrawable.

33
00:01:49,625 --> 00:01:51,075
Challenge two, placeable routes.

34
00:01:51,125 --> 00:02:08,700
A route the exchange would reject is worthless, so every reduction is sized in the zero point zero one SOL lot, priced at your own taker rate, checked against the ten-dollar minimum; the rehearsal walks the level-two book and builds the order in the exchange's wire shape.

35
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:10,575
Challenge three, real Solana legs.

36
00:02:10,625 --> 00:02:23,700
The sell is the real Jupiter swap, the Kamino leg is the real withdraw instruction set; both run through simulateTransaction, and I read the USDC account out of the simulation to report what would arrive.

37
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:29,700
Read-only by design, integer-cent arithmetic, fail-closed: a bad or stale input stops planning instead of guessing.

38
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:38,575
The same engine from the terminal: one command prints the same pre-flight report, so a bot or a CI job can run it.

39
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,575
Next is execution behind the same check:

40
00:02:44,625 --> 00:02:50,950
Phantom signs the Solana legs, a Hyperliquid builder code routes the short, CCTP brings the USDC home.

41
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,200
Today nothing is signed or sent.
